{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"d1d157ef-42c4-407b-b317-a9e655f86d0d","step_index":34,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.285453577,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"grep -rn \"auth-client\" audit/findings/ \u0026\u0026 grep -rn \"error envelope\" audit/findings/ -i"},"output":"Created At: 2026-11-22T21:21:47+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-22T21:21:47+05:30\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\naudit/findings/F-097.md:39:   - `client/src/lib/auth-client.ts` uses native `fetch()` for `/api/auth/sign-in/email` and `/api/auth/sign-out`, bypassing Axios interceptors and error logging.\r\naudit/findings/F-097.md:94:3. Standardize `auth-client.ts` to use `apiClient` or migrate all requests to a unified `fetch` wrapper.\r\naudit/findings/F-097.md:40:4. **Mismatched Error Envelopes**:\r\naudit/findings/F-034.md:1:# Finding F-034: Inconsistent Error Envelope Shape, Unhandled Postgres Violations, and Information Leakage via Stack Traces\r\naudit/findings/F-034.md:4:**Title**: Server lacks consistent error envelope (missing code, fieldErrors, requestId), leaks internal Prisma schema details and stack traces, and triggers client UI error masking  \r\naudit/findings/F-034.md:54:Zero uniform error envelope. Complete absence of `requestId` and `fieldErrors`. Stack trace leakage on 413 and foreign key errors. Total masking of server errors in client UI toasts.\r\naudit/findings/F-025.md:13:`request-id -\u003e security headers -\u003e CORS -\u003e body size limits and parsers -\u003e request logging -\u003e rate limit -\u003e session/auth -\u003e permission check -\u003e input validation -\u003e idempotency -\u003e handler -\u003e not-found -\u003e error envelope`.\r\naudit/findings/F-025.md:14:All unmapped routes must return a consistent JSON error envelope `{ \"error\": \"Not Found\" }` with status 404. Body parser `PayloadTooLargeError` must return HTTP 413 Content Too Large. Every request must be traceable with a correlation ID (`X-Request-Id`).\r\naudit/findings/F-045.md:14:  Every screen must provide structured loading feedback using layout skeletons (not spinner-only boxes) to maintain layout stability (zero CLS) and communicate content hierarchy before data arrives. When an error occurs, the screen must display what happened, recommended user action, and the specific Request ID (`x-request-id` from server error envelope) to enable support debugging.\r\n"}}}
